{
  "subject": "Java",
  "title": "Chapter 9 : OOPs",
  "createdAt": "2026-08-02T08:10:10.266Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-08-02T08:26:09.072Z",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Object Oriented Programming"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " is a way of writing programs by organising code into "
        },
        {
          "text": "objects",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " that contain both "
        },
        {
          "text": "data (fields) ",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and "
        },
        {
          "text": "behavior (methods)",
          "marks": [
            "bold"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Without OOP (Procedural Style)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Data and functions are kept separate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "In this, code is written as just sequence of instructions from top to bottom. "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "//Loose data and functions\nString name = \"Bruno\";\nbark(name);"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Data "
            },
            {
              "text": "name",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": " exists separately."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Functions "
            },
            {
              "text": "bark()",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": " operate on that data."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "As programs grow, keeping related data and behavior together becomes harder."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "With OOP"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Data and behavior are grouped together inside an object."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "Dog d1 = new Dog();\n\nd1.name = \"Bruno\";  // Data\nd1.bark();          // Behavior"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Here, d1 is a self-contained object that owns:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Its own data (name, age)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Its own behavior (bark())"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
